WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.482
Now we bring several professional practices together in a small project.

00:00:04.482 --> 00:00:07.442
The data contains messy order records.

00:00:07.442 --> 00:00:10.662
One amount is a valid number stored as text.

00:00:10.662 --> 00:00:13.147
Another amount is N A.

00:00:13.147 --> 00:00:18.207
The status labels also have inconsistent spacing and capitalization.

00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:20.747
We write two helper functions.

00:00:20.747 --> 00:00:24.737
The parse_amount function tries to convert a value to a float.

00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:27.992
If conversion fails, it returns None.

00:00:27.992 --> 00:00:33.987
The normalize_status function removes extra spaces and converts the text to lowercase.

00:00:33.987 --> 00:00:36.247
Then we loop through the orders.

00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:40.902
If the amount is valid, we append a cleaned record to clean_orders.

00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:44.067
Run the cell and inspect the cleaned list.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:50.122
Notice that the invalid order amount is excluded, and the status labels are standardized.

00:00:50.122 --> 00:00:56.482
This is a realistic pattern: define small helper functions, clean records step by step,

00:00:56.482 --> 00:00:57.896
and inspect the result.
